+        <div class="mp-stage" id="mcpStage"><noscript><div class="crawl-text"><p>A recorded session with the kshana-mcp server (Model Context Protocol, engine v0.40.0): the assistant lists the 52 tools, validates <code>clock-holdover.toml</code> (valid: detected scenario kind `clock`) and runs it: scenario 5ba83a232b94 | quantum holdover 6600s p95 1.20e-4ns integrity 1.000 security n/a (no attack) | classical holdover 2610s p95 19.7ns integrity 1.000 security n/a (no attack).</p><ul><li><code>animate_scenario</code>: Run a Kshana scenario and return its time series as an animation.</li><li><code>assess_receiver_log</code>: Assess a real GNSS receiver log for trust: read a u-blox UBX, RINEX 3 (optionally with broadcast navigation, which adds the engine&#x27;s own fix, RAIM and a clock-aided monitor), Android GnssLogger or NMEA log, run the trust monitors (carrier-to-noise density drop, AGC, jamming indicator, loss of lock, position jump, RAIM, clock) against a calibration baseline, and return when and why the receiver stopped being trustworthy.</li><li><code>assess_vessel_log</code>: Assess a vessel&#x27;s NMEA 0183 log as a batch run (`kshana receiver-trust` with `[platform] kind = &quot;vessel&quot;`): the score model, the monitors that ran and every epoch&#x27;s 0-100 score with its deductions, its satellite geometry (good, degraded, unknown) with a `label` (good, fair, poor) on every epoch, geometry deducting only when poor, and a class on every deduction (geometry, environment, inconsistency), with `geometry_model` (thresholds, the cap and floor in force, and provenance) and `geometry_summary`.</li><li><code>assess_vessel_stream</code>: Score a bounded excerpt of a vessel&#x27;s NMEA 0183 stream the way `kshana receiver-trust live` scores it, and return per-epoch trust state (calibrating, nominal, degraded, untrusted) and 0-100 score with the monitors that deducted (live JSON-lines schema 1.3: each epoch carries `position`, an `advisory` statement that the outp