 <div class="ref-card"><h3>GNSS beyond the constellation: the Space Service Volume and past it</h3><div class="ref-meta"><span>Nav-signal performance</span><span>Modelled</span><span>ICG SSV booklet tables, pre-registered; most bars NOT MET (xval/gnss-ssv/RESULTS.md)</span></div><p>For a spacecraft on a sphere (the global shell of the ICG Space Service Volume booklet) or on a Keplerian trajectory from LEO to lunar transfer, counts per constellation (GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, BDS, QZSS, NavIC) and for all together the signals above a C/N0 threshold: availability of one and of four signals, longest outage, received C/N0, dilution of precision, and main-lobe against sidelobe links. Transmit patterns are the booklet's, a parametric stand-in or one you supply; a limb-ray ionosphere, plasmasphere and atmosphere model and a weak-signal receiver design are optional; an onboard GNSS filter for high and lunar-transfer orbits and formation relative navigation are included. MODELLED: compared with the booklet's tables under a pre-registration committed before the run, the minimum-radiated-power constants and the lunar bar agree, the other bars are NOT MET under the pre-registered reading (almost all through the booklet's inconsistent GLONASS beam angle), and the parametric sidelobe stand-in does not reproduce the measured GPS panel patterns.</p><p><a href="/studio/?scenario=gnss-ssv-shell&amp;tab=overview">Run gnss-ssv-shell.toml in Kshana Studio</a></p></div>
 <div class="ref-card"><h3>Lunar orbit and surface as navigation and geodetic infrastructure</h3><div class="ref-meta"><span>Lunar &amp; cislunar</span><span>Modelled</span><span>numpy/scipy oracles of the numerics; three pre-registered bars NOT MET (xval/lunar-infra/RESULTS.md)</span></div><p>Five studies in a restricted three-body model: an onboard Earth-GNSS orbit determination in a near-rectilinear halo orbit against an independent ground range and range-rate determination; joint surface-station and orbiter carrier-phase integer ambiguity fixing (LAMBDA); the Fisher information of a seven-parameter lunar datum with and without orbiter-to-surface ranges; GNSS, VLBI and laser-ranging offsets against the local tie; and sensitivity to the lunar tidal and libration parameters. MODELLED with illustrative inputs: the numerics are checked against independent numpy and scipy programs, not the physics. Under the pre-registered bars, three are NOT MET: an injected force error is not detected at the stated rate (C3), the bootstrapped success rate differs from the numpy oracle by 1.7e-6 against a bar of 1e-9 (Q3), and adding a ranging family does not always lower the pseudo-inverse trace (G3, trace half).</p><p><a href="/studio/?scenario=lunar-infrastructure-od-consistency&amp;tab=overview">Run lunar-infrastructure-od-consistency.toml in Kshana Studio</a></p></div>
