ial to the geodetic local level (up to 0.31 m HPL and 0.14 m VPL at 16 deg N)</td><td><code>araim_reference (add_v42_protection_levels, add_v42_protection_levels_ecef); raim (snapshot_raim, snapshot_raim_fde, araim_raim, araim_dual_raim, solution_separation_raim); sbas (sbas_protection_level); lunar</code></td></tr><tr><td>Orbit propagation &amp; determination</td><td>SGP4/SDP4, Cowell 6-DOF + perturbations, batch/sequential OD</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>AIAA 2006-6753 SGP4 verification vectors</td><td><code>sgp4, propagator, orbit_determination, precise_od</code></td></tr><tr><td>Numerical Cowell propagator &amp; force model</td><td>Cowell numerical propagator with a hierarchical force model (two-body, J2–J6 zonal, Sun/Moon third-body, cannonball SRP, exponential drag); RK4 step-doubling / DP5(4) / DOP853</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>Orekit 12.2 (CS GROUP, Apache-2.0) NumericalPropagator/DormandPrince853 — an independent library, a different integrator and spherical-harmonic recursion. The conservative tiers (two-body → J2–J6 zonal → Sun/Moon third-body → cannonball SRP) agree to sub-metre over a 24 h arc, validating the integrator + force algebra; the drag tier and the absolute Sun/Moon-ephemeris / density input fidelity stay MODELLED (characterisation only)</td><td><code>propagator, forces</code></td></tr><tr><td>Oblate-Earth SRP shadow (opt-in)</td><td>SRP lit fraction with the WGS-84 ellipsoid as the occulting body (apparent Earth radius from the ellipsoid limb towards the Sun, dual-disk lens formula; srp_shadow::oblate_conical_shadow), opt-in on the Cowell force model through propagator::ForceModel::srp_shadow (default: the spherical conical shadow, unchanged)</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>Orekit 12.2 (Apache-2.0) SolarRadiationPressure.getLightingRatio with a WGS-84 and a spherical OneAxisEllipsoid occulting body, run as a separate program with the Sun fixed at the same inertial position. Bars pre-registered in xval/srp-oblate-shadow-orekit/PREREGISTRATION.md (6d6d269c): 1e-6 on both, and a &gt; 1e-2 oblate-vs-sphere spread; all met. The ellipsoid axis is the inertial z axis on both sides (no precession-nutation)</td><td><code>srp_shadow, forces (srp_accel_with_lit_fraction), propagator</code></td></tr><tr><td>Box-wing and ECOM2 solar radiation pressure, with partials (opt-in)</td><td>Non-cannonball SRP: a box-wing flat-plate model (Vallado eq. 8-44; single-sided body panels, sun-pointing wings) with the Galileo FOC, IOV and IOV end-of-life tables of the GSC satellite metadata, in nominal GNSS yaw steering, with analytic partials for the radiation factor and every panel's specular and diffuse coefficients; and the ECOM2 empirical model (D2/B1) with its partials. The box-wing is opt-in on the Cowell propagator (propagator::ForceModel::box_wing_srp, setting its srp_boxwing field) and on the precise orbit-determination model (precise_od::PreciseForceModel::box_wing_srp), replacing the cannonball term with cr as the radiation factor; both default to None, leaving every existing path byte-identical. ECOM2 is not wired into a force model</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>Orekit 12.2 (Apache-2.0) BoxAndSolarArraySpacecraft with FixedPanel and PointingPanel, SolarRadiationPressure(dRef = 1 au, pRef = 1361/c), GenericGNSS nominal yaw and ECOM2(nD = 2, nB = 1), run as a separate program with the Sun at fixed inertial positions; the radiation-factor derivative from Hipparchus Gradient, per-panel derivatives as central differences of Orekit (Orekit has none). Bars pre-registered in xval/srp-boxwing-orekit/PREREGISTRATION.md (e59df6bf), before any Orekit output existed: 1e-12 relative (1e-11 end to end, 1e-9 for the differences); all met (RESULTS.md). VALIDATED covers the model evaluation only: the GSC tables are transcribed inputs, and the adequacy of a box-wing for real Galileo orbits, thermal re-emission, the modified low-beta yaw law and eclipse turns are not covered; the Galileo SRP prediction stays MODELLED</td><td><code>srp_boxwing, propagator, precise_od</code></td></tr><tr><td>Solar limb-darkened SRP shadow (opt-in)</td><td>SRP lit fraction as the un-occulted fraction of the limb-darkened solar flux (Eddington-approximation law I(mu)/I(1) = 2/5 + 3/5 mu, Gauss-Legendre quadrature) over a spherical or WGS-84 Earth (srp_shadow::limb_darkened_shadow, the ShadowModel variant OblateEarthLimbDarkened)</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>None external: Orekit 12.2 has no limb-darkened lighting ratio. Checked against closed forms of the same law only</td><td><code>srp_shadow</code></td></tr><tr><td>NRLMSISE-00 thermospheric density</td><td>A port of the NRLMSISE-00 empirical thermosphere (gtd7 and gtd7d: species densities, total mass density with anomalous oxygen, temperatures; the 24 switches; daily-Ap and 3-hourly ap-array modes) from the public-domain C version of the NRL Fortran</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>pymsis 0.13.0 (MIT) version=0, which runs the NRL Fortran GTD7D in single precision, and the NRLMSISE-00 C port (release 20190709, public domain) compiled as a separate program, plus the C distribution's 17 published test outputs. Bars pre-registered in xval/nrlmsise00-pymsis/PREREGISTRATION.md (e90ae26a) before the port existed; all met (RESULTS.md). Validates the port, not the model's accuracy against measured density</td><td><code>nrlmsise00</code></td></tr><tr><td>NRLMSISE-00 drag-density tier (opt-in)</td><td>forces::DensityModel (Exponential default, Nrlmsise00 { f107a, f107, ap }) and propagator::ForceModel::drag_density: quadratic drag against the co-rotating atmosphere with the NRLMSISE-00 density at the WGS-84 geodetic point (Earth rotation angle with UT1 = TT, local solar time UT + lon/15), constant space weather per model; default off and bit-identical</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>Orekit 12.2 (Apache-2.0) NumericalPropagator/DormandPrince853 with DragForce over Orekit's own NRLMSISE00 implementation, run as a separate program with the same Earth-rotation-angle frame, WGS-84 shape, local-solar-time conventi