on 3, with the RINEX antenna heights) giving the reference baseline; bars pre-registered in tests/fixtures/gnss_wettzell_2025055/PREREGISTRATION_RTK.md before the code was written. Short baseline only: no ionospheric or tropospheric double differences are modelled</td><td><code>rtk_real (run_rtk), lambda (resolve)</code></td></tr><tr><td>PPP receiver-clock time solution against the IGS final station clock</td><td>The receiver clock estimated by the static float PPP filter on real dual-frequency GPS code and phase with IGS final orbits and clocks: a time transfer from the receiver to IGS time, the PPP iono-free time solution.</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>The IGS final combined clock for station WTZR (AR records of IGS0OPSFIN_20250550000_01D_05M_CLK, SHA-256 d19f3d45...993d, a combination of several analysis centres' network solutions; IGS products, free use with attribution); bars pre-registered in xval/ppp-time/PREREGISTRATION.md before any comparison; all held on the first run. WHAT IS NOT: one station and one two-hour converged window; IGS time, not UTC(k); the constant offset includes receiver code biases and is bounded, not calibrated; no Circular T traceability.</td><td><code>ppp_real (run_ppp, PppEpoch::clock_m)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Float precise point positioning on real RINEX observations</td><td>Static float PPP extended Kalman filter on real dual-frequency GPS code and carrier phase with IGS final orbits and clocks: ionosphere-free combination, satellite and receiver antenna offsets (receiver variations), solid Earth tide, phase wind-up, Shapiro delay, estimated zenith wet delay, per-arc float ambiguities with geometry-free / Melbourne-Wübbena slip detection</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>Published ITRF2020 coordinate of WTZR (IGN ITRF2020_GNSS.SSC, solution 3, propagated with its velocity) — bars pre-registered in tests/fixtures/gnss_wettzell_2025055/PREREGISTRATION_PPP.md before the filter was written; development on the co-located station WTZZ only. Not modelled: ocean loading, satellite PCV, integer ambiguity resolution</td><td><code>ppp_real (run_ppp, parse_antex_receiver, solid_tide_ecef, phase_windup)</code></td></tr><tr><td>RINEX 4 navigation file reading</td><td>RINEX 4.00-4.02 navigation files: <code>&gt; EPH</code> records of GPS LNAV, Galileo I/NAV and F/NAV, BeiDou D1/D2 and QZSS LNAV decoded into the broadcast-ephemeris type; CNAV, CNV1-3, FDMA, SBAS, STO, EOP and ION records skipped to the next record header; a record whose header names another satellite, or a truncated record, refused</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>The same day's RINEX 3 merged broadcast file of the IGS (published data, written by a different file generator from the same broadcast messages); bars pre-registered in tests/fixtures/brdc_rinex4_2026200/PREREGISTRATION.md (589b7c9) before the first run</td><td><code>rinex (parse_nav, parse_nav_with)</code></td></tr><tr><td>RINEX 4 observation file reading</td><td>RINEX 4.0x observation headers (DOI, LICENSE OF USE, STATION INFORMATION, MERGED FILE; labels matched in columns 61-80 for version 4 and later) and epoch records</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>Format conformance on a real published RINEX 4.00 file (values read back equal the file's printed literals) and a specification-derived header; no independent reader was run, so MODELLED</td><td><code>rinex_obs (parse_obs)</code></td></tr><tr><td>BeiDou GEO broadcast satellite position</td><td>BDS-SIS-ICD-B1I v3.0 §5.2.4.12 geostationary-satellite position from a broadcast ephemeris (inertial-like frame, then Rz(Ω̇e·tk)·Rx(−5°)), opt-in through the include_beidou_geo field of NavParseOptions, so the default reader still skips GEOs</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>Pre-registered (589b7c9, 3446949) against an IGS MGEX precise orbit with the GEOs; no such product was reachable from the session that built it, so the comparison is pending and the row is MODELLED (checked against the published nominal GEO slots only)</td><td><code>rinex (RinexEphemeris::sv_position_ecef_bds_geo, NavParseOptions)</code></td></tr><tr><td>SP3 precise-clock interpolation</td><td>Satellite clock offset between the tabulated SP3 clock nodes by linear interpolation over the two bracketing valid nodes (the RTKLIB pephclk scheme; bad-clock sentinel skipped), and the same nodes fed to the precise-product chain as RINEX-clock-equivalent records</td><td>VALIDATED</td><td>IGS final 30 s satellite clock combination (IGS0OPSFIN 30S CLK, 2025-02-24): published clock estimates at the query instants, not interpolated from the SP3; bars pre-registered in tests/fixtures/sp3_clock_igs_oracle/PREREGISTRATION.md before the first run (RMS 0.15 ns, p95 0.30 ns, node median 1e-12 s, discrimination 2x)</td><td><code>sp3 (Sp3File::clock_s, clock_nodes), precise_products (ClockRinex::from_sp3)</code></td></tr><tr><td>Carrier-phase tightly coupled GNSS/INS with float ambiguities</td><td>Error-state EKF over 15 INS states, a two-state receiver clock and one float carrier ambiguity per tracked satellite; pseudorange, carrier phase and optional range rate from an SGP4 Walker constellation (light-time and Sagnac), Klobuchar and Saastamoinen/Niell corrections applied in the loop at the filter's own position; time-differenced-carrier slip detection with a per-satellite threshold widened by the velocity uncertainty; ambiguity re-initialisation on slips and re-acquisition</td><td>MODELLED</td><td>Internal consistency: the measurements are synthesised from the models the filter uses (χ² NEES/NIS over seeds, a noise-free convergence, slip injection). MODELLED; no real receiver data or third-party filter is compared</td><td><code>fusion::carrier_tc (run_carrier_tc, CarrierTcCfg), fusion::trajectory (truth_epochs)</code></td></tr><tr><td>GNSS/INS maritime, rail and aviation packs with a tight-coupling option</td><td>Three gnss-ins scenarios on the trajectory library (a vessel weaving at 8 m/s with a five-minute outage; a train through a two-satellite cutting and a tunnel; an aircraft whose