 <h2 id="unreleased"><a href="https://github.com/AshfordeOU/kshana/compare/v0.30.0...HEAD">Unreleased</a><a class="anchor" href="#unreleased" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<h3 id="added">Added<a class="anchor" href="#added" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
+<ul>
+<li>RTCM SSR reader (<code>kshana::rtcm_ssr</code>) reads the IGS SSR format (RTCM 4076): orbit, clock, combined, high-rate clock, code
+bias, phase bias with yaw and URA for GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, QZSS, BeiDou and SBAS, and the global ionosphere (201). Every
+field of the 11 messages in pyrtcm 1.2.0&#39;s public IGS sample stream matches the values pyrtcm records; the message kinds
+missing from that stream are checked against hand-built frames only. MODELLED.</li>
+<li><code>kshana.obs/1</code> correction records, and <code>kshana obs convert --format rtcm-ssr</code>: an RTCM 3 stream&#39;s SSR corrections (RTCM
+and IGS SSR) become one record per satellite of each message, with <code>t_s</code> on GPS time. Every value of the 676 records from
+the three public sample streams equals pyrtcm&#39;s after a round trip through <code>obs check</code>; <code>obs check</code> counts corrections.
+MODELLED; the limits are in <code>docs/design/evidence/r1-1-rtcm-ssr/RESULTS.md</code>.</li>
+<li><code>leo-signal</code>: GPS L2C as a public reference preset (<code>gps-l2c</code>, from IS-GPS-200N: 1227.60 MHz, CM and CL time-multiplexed,
+−160.0 dBW) and as a GNSS victim in the compatibility analysis, so a LEO-PNT design is scored against L2C and L2C against it.
+MODELLED: checked against the CM and CL codes in <code>iq::signals::gps</code> and the BPSK closed forms only.</li>
+<li><code>kshana::solid_tide</code>: the IERS Conventions (2010) solid Earth tide displacement, Steps 1 and 2 (degree 2 and 3, the
+latitude, out-of-phase and frequency-dependence terms), written from the Conventions text. MODELLED; not yet used by PPP. The
+comparison with the IERS test cases waits for its pre-registration&#39;s sign-off (R1.4).</li>
+<li><code>kshana::bias_sinex</code>: a Bias-SINEX 1.00 reader (DSB, ISB and OSB; code and phase; offsets, slopes and open intervals), and a
+lookup of a satellite&#39;s observable-specific bias at a time. On two public files every data line is read with the values
+printed. Both files&#39; headers state a count of estimates that differs from their data lines. MODELLED; applying the biases
+in PPP is item R1.3.</li>
+<li><code>kshana::tip_and_cue</code> (row M2, library): Walker star RF and optical layers on 550 km sun-synchronous orbits over the 996
+Baltic sea points (<code>data/tip-and-cue/baltic_sea_points.csv</code>, from Natural Earth), access intervals per point, and the
+revisit, full-area refresh and RF-to-optical reaction figures; public helpers for the area grid, the sea mask, the primary
+RF layer and one of its planes. Bar M2-B0 met: 1 283 access intervals equal the independent oracle&#39;s to the second. The
+<code>tip-and-cue</code> scenario kind follows with the site rebuild. MODELLED.</li>
+</ul>
+<h3 id="fixed">Fixed<a class="anchor" href="#fixed" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
+<ul>
+<li>An SBF log cut inside its last block, or with a stray <code>$@</code> sync whose declared length runs past the end, no longer makes
+<code>kshana obs convert</code> and the receiver-trust SBF reader loop forever: the blocks are framed by Kshana and the unfinished one
+counts as one skipped record (<code>tests/receiver_trust_sbf.rs</code>).</li>
+</ul>
+<h3 id="revisions">Revisions<a class="anchor" href="#revisions" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h3>
+<ul>
+<li>Mars short-arc orbit determination, run 2: since portable maths (0.36), the fit takes 11 Jacobian evaluations, B3 is 0.359 km
+and B4 is 0.523 km (were 12, 0.362 and 0.527). Every verdict is unchanged; B2 stays NOT MET and the row stays MODELLED. The
+data-gated test was missed by the 0.36 re-baseline. See <code>docs/revisions/CAP30-run2-portable-math-rebaseline.md</code>.</li>
+</ul>
