+<h2 id="adding-an-adapter">Adding an adapter<a class="anchor" href="#adding-an-adapter" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<p>A device or log format that Kshana can read through a mapping file is added as an adapter: one folder
+under <code>adapters/</code>, with no change to the engine. The folder holds an <code>adapter.toml</code>, the mapping file, a
+sample you may share (no customer or personal data), and a conformance vector with its expected output.
+Run <code>kshana connect adapters check adapters</code> before opening the pull request: it validates the manifest
+and runs the vector, and CI runs the same check. The details are in <a href="https://github.com/ashfordeOU/kshana/blob/main/docs/ADAPTERS.md">docs/ADAPTERS.md</a>.
+The licensing above applies to adapters too.</p>
