+<p><strong>ASTERIX CAT021 (air-traffic ADS-B reports), library.</strong> <code>kshana::asterix_cat021::read</code> reads a
+recording of EUROCONTROL ASTERIX Category 021 data blocks (edition 2.6 items). <code>to_adsb_csv</code> writes the
+CSV above for a stated UTC day, because CAT021 carries the time of day only.</p>
+<ul>
+<li>NIC is written only for MOPS version 1 or later; version 0 sends NUCp in that field, which is a
+different scale.</li>
+<li>NACp comes from the first extension of the quality indicators.</li>
+<li>Positions use the high-resolution item when present.</li>
+<li>Every item of the profile is stepped over by its own length rule, so one unused field does not lose
+the rest of the block.</li>
+<li>Checked against an independent encoder (<code>tests/asterix_cat021.rs</code>); no public recording has been
+checked yet.</li>
+</ul>
 <p><strong>adsb.lol readsb history, read directly.</strong> The daily archives are a split tar of readsb
 trace files. Extract one as the publisher describes (concatenate the parts, <code>tar -xf -</code>),
 then give Kshana the extracted directory, a single <code>trace_full_*.json</code> file, or a CSV:</p>
