+<h2 id="live-feeds-from-a-local-receiver-interference-map-record">Live feeds from a local receiver (<code>interference-map record</code>)<a class="anchor" href="#live-feeds-from-a-local-receiver-interference-map-record" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<pre data-lang="shell"><code class="hljs language-bash"><span class="hljs-comment"># ADS-B: the aircraft.json readsb or dump1090-fa writes (--write-json), read every second</span>
+kshana interference-map record --<span class="hljs-built_in">source</span> adsb --from /run/readsb/aircraft.json --out adsb-today.csv
+
+<span class="hljs-comment"># AIS: AIS-catcher (or any AIS receiver) sending NMEA over UDP or TCP, or a pipe</span>
+AIS-catcher -u 127.0.0.1 10110 &amp;
+kshana interference-map record --<span class="hljs-built_in">source</span> ais --from udp:10110 --out ais-today.csv</code></pre>
+<p><code>record</code> writes the reports into the CSV formats above as they arrive, flushing each row, so the file is
+the input of <code>locate</code>, <code>adsb</code> and <code>ais</code>: a live run and its replay read the same rows. The output file
+must not exist yet (nothing is overwritten); stop with Ctrl-C or <code>--max-seconds</code>.</p>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>ADS-B</strong> reads readsb <code>aircraft.json</code> snapshots: a file read every <code>--poll-s</code> seconds (default 1), or
+one snapshot per line from <code>-</code>, <code>tcp:host:port</code> or a file. An aircraft becomes a row when its position
+is newer than its last row (time <code>now - seen_pos</code>, to the millisecond). Aircraft on the ground and
+aircraft without a position are not written. <code>type</code> is kept as <code>source_type</code>, so non-ADS-B positions
+(MLAT, TIS-B) are excluded later exactly as in an archive.</li>
+<li><strong>AIS</strong> reads <code>!AIVDM</code> and <code>!AIVDO</code> sentences from <code>-</code>, <code>tcp:host:port</code>, <code>udp:port</code> (bound to the
+loopback interface; <code>udp:addr:port</code> to listen wider) or a file. The checksum is checked and fragments are
+joined; position reports (types 1, 2, 3, 18 and 19, ITU-R M.1371 layout) become rows. The time is the
+NMEA 4 TAG block <code>c:</code> field when the sentence has one, otherwise the time it arrived.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>The identifiers are written as received (ICAO address, MMSI) into the operator&#39;s own file, which is sent
+nowhere; the map and region readers hash them with a random salt, as for any other input.
+<code>tests/interference_map_live.rs</code> checks that AIS over TCP gives the same file as the same sentences read
+from a file, that each readsb position is written once, and that <code>locate</code> reads both files.</p>
 <h2 id="emitter-region-interference-map-locate">Emitter region (<code>interference-map locate</code>)<a class="anchor" href="#emitter-region-interference-map-locate" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
 <p><code>kshana interference-map locate</code> estimates <strong>where an interference source can be</strong> from the same open ADS-B or
 AIS reports: a region at stated confidence levels, a centroid with an uncertainty ellipse, and the sessions in
 time. It never returns a bare point. <strong>MODELLED</strong> (ledger row <code>VM-bc70cb57</code>): the physics is textbook radio
 line of sight, the credibility of the regions is conditional on the model, and the only external check is the
-Jammertest comparison pre-registered in <span class="not-pushed" title="In the repository branch these docs come from; not yet on GitHub"><code>emitter-region/PREREGISTRATION.md</code></span>.
+Jammertest comparison pre-registered in <a href="https://github.com/ashfordeOU/kshana/blob/main/docs/emitter-region/PREREGISTRATION.md"><code>emitter-region/PREREGISTRATION.md</code></a>.
 Publishing emitter regions in the public observatory is a separate owner decision and is <strong>off</strong>: the observatory
 does not read this module, and a test pins that.</p>
 <pre data-lang="text"><code class="hljs">kshana interference-map locate input.csv --source adsb --dataset adsb-lol --out regions/
