 <li><strong>MODELLED</strong> The three terms a differential correction picks up between the epoch it is computed at and the epoch it is used at, each previously left as unmodelled headroom:. Oracle (InternalConsistency): Closed-form identities and self-consistency: the uniform-quantizer step²/12 variance, the exact (GᵀG)⁻¹GᵀRG(GᵀG)⁻¹ covariance propagation collapsing to σ·PDOP for equal σ, the survey term&#39;s 1:1 transfer as a consequence of û_user ≈ û_ref, and switching-off quadrature closure. The PDOP cross-check against orbit::dop shares the [−û, 1] normal matrix, so it is a consistency check and is labelled as one rather than an in</li>
