+<h1 id="tip-and-cue"><code>tip-and-cue</code> (scenario kind)</h1>
+<p>Scenario kind of the engine v0.40.0, family <a href="/docs/kinds-space-rf-survey">Space RF survey</a>. Advisory: analysis output from a research and engineering tool, not type-approved navigation equipment and not a safety-of-life service. Every label here is the engine&#39;s or the verification matrix&#39;s; a kind is MODELLED unless the matrix says otherwise (how a label is earned: the README&#39;s Evidence section).</p>
+<h2 id="what-it-does">What it does<a class="anchor" href="#what-it-does" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<p>MODELLED revisit and tip-and-cue latency of a two-layer maritime survey over the Baltic Sea: an RF survey layer and an optical layer, each a Walker star pattern of 550 km sun-synchronous orbits propagated with the secular J2 drift on a spherical Earth, with an elevation mask for the RF layer and an off-nadir field of regard (and optionally daylight) for the optical layer. Reports R, the area-weighted mean gap between RF accesses per point; F, the mean wait until every sea point has been in view; and Q, the mean wait from an RF access to an optical look, each with its median, 95th percentile and largest value. Geometry and timing only: no detection, weather or tasking latency. A cross-check of published simulation figures, never a validation.</p>
+<p>One run of <code>scenarios/tip-and-cue-short.toml</code> summarises as: tip-and-cue: 1 cases over 996 area points (minutes)
+rf-16-optical-16: revisit 25.8, full-area refresh 15.3, RF-to-optical reaction 22.6</p>
