+<h2 id="evidence">Evidence<a class="anchor" href="#evidence" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<p>No matrix row names this kind by name; the label on its result is the engine&#39;s own, above.</p>
+<p>The rows the run itself exercised, with the oracle the matrix gives each (the public sources are named there):</p>
+<ul>
+<li><strong>MODELLED</strong> Deterministic, scenario-hashed, SBOM + cross-platform golden gates. Oracle (ExternalDataset): SBOM conformance to the official CycloneDX 1.5 JSON Schema (+ valid SPDX identifiers) — an external published standard, zero validation errors over the full dependency graph; the FoM-determinism / byte-reproducibility part remains a pinned self-consistency check, so the row stays MODELLED</li>
+</ul>
+<h2 id="limitations">Limitations<a class="anchor" href="#limitations" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
+<p>What the run&#39;s own report says is not modelled or not validated:</p>
+<ul>
+<li>MODELLED: revisit, full-area refresh and RF-to-optical reaction of a two-layer survey from stated Walker star layers on 550 km sun-synchronous orbits (secular J2), spherical Earth, stated fields of regard; geometry and timing only, no detection, weather or tasking latency; a cross-check of published simulation figures, never a validation (result <code>label</code>)</li>
+<li>MODELLED revisit and tip-and-cue latency of a two-layer maritime survey over the Baltic Sea: an RF survey layer and an optical layer, each a Walker star pattern of 550 km sun-synchronous orbits propagated with the secular J2 drift on a spherical Earth, with an elevation mask for the RF layer and an off-nadir field of regard (and optionally daylight) for the optical layer. (kind catalogue (<code>kshana kinds --json</code>))</li>
+<li>A short tip-and-cue run: the M2 primary 16-satellite RF layer cueing its optical layer over the Baltic Sea for 2 days at a 60 s step (fast; for the full pre-registered run see tip-and-cue-baltic-m2.toml). Geometry and timing only; MODELLED. (scenario file comment, lines 1 to 3)</li>
+<li>Reproducibility &amp; software assurance is MODELLED, not validated: a sub-claim is externally checked, but the whole capability composes modelled pieces, so the capability stays Modelled. (verification matrix (docs/MODELLED-RATIONALE.md))</li>
+</ul>
