+<p>An NMEA 2000 network is read through a SocketCAN interface: <code>kshana sensor-live --kind n2k</code> turns the
+position, course and speed, heading and system-time groups into NMEA 0183 sentences (see
+<a href="/docs/machine-inputs"><code>MACHINE-INPUTS.md</code></a>), which this command reads as it reads any other:</p>
+<pre data-lang="shell"><code class="hljs language-bash">candump -L can0 | kshana sensor-live --kind n2k --from - | kshana receiver-trust live session.toml</code></pre>
 <p>The session is the same <code>session.toml</code> as a batch run, with a <code>[platform]</code> table that declares
 <code>kind = &quot;vessel&quot;</code>; its <code>[log]</code> table is not needed. Serial ports are not opened directly yet:
 read the port with the tool you already use (<code>stty</code> and <code>cat</code>, a terminal server, a
