@@ -192,6 +192,10 @@ figures of merit with their provenance and their VALIDATED or MODELLED label.</p
 <td>Score a receiver log against that schedule (<code>kshana jammertest score</code>): per test the detection latency, missed alarms and time to recover, and the false alarms outside every slot. Text logs as <code>log</code>, binary (<code>ubx</code>, <code>sbf</code>) as <code>log_base64</code>. A signed pack needs a key: command line. Advisory only; MODELLED.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
+<td><code>referee_location_score</code></td>
+<td>Score where a monitoring network said interference came from (<code>kshana jammertest locate-score</code>, row B2): per report the attributed event, the geodesic error and region containment and size; per event and pooled, error percentiles, coverage per level, time to first location and time to locate; false locations per hour. Checks arithmetic, not any locator&#39;s accuracy.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
 <td><code>create_evidence_pack</code></td>
 <td>A signed evidence pack for a window of a vessel&#39;s log (<code>kshana receiver-trust evidence</code>): the raw log bytes for the window, configuration, per-epoch results and reasons, a summary page, and a manifest with every SHA-256 and a hash chain, signed with Ed25519. The signing seed is never returned or logged; without one a one-time key is used, so the pack proves integrity, not identity. A technical record, not a legal opinion. See <a href="/docs/evidence-packs"><code>docs/EVIDENCE-PACKS.md</code></a>.</td>
 </tr>
@@ -212,6 +216,14 @@ figures of merit with their provenance and their VALIDATED or MODELLED label.</p
 <td>A GNSS interference map from ADS-B or AIS position reports as CSV text (at most 4 MiB): one <code>kshana-interference-map/v1</code> GeoJSON per UTC day, aggregate only (no identifiers, cells under 5 distinct aircraft or vessels withheld), with the dataset licence embedded. A degraded cell does not identify interference as the cause; not a forecast. MODELLED. See <a href="/docs/interference-map"><code>docs/INTERFERENCE-MAP.md</code></a>.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr>
+<td><code>interference_emitter_regions</code></td>
+<td>Estimated emitter regions from ADS-B or AIS reports as CSV text (at most 4 MiB): regions at stated confidence levels with a centroid and an uncertainty ellipse, never a bare point; aggregate only. A region is not the position of anyone and not a finding of the cause. MODELLED. See <a href="/docs/interference-map"><code>docs/INTERFERENCE-MAP.md</code></a>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
+<td><code>connect_map</code></td>
+<td>Kshana Connect without code: a <code>kshana.connect/1</code> mapping and a station (TOML text) applied to a log (text, at most 4 MiB), returning <code>kshana.obs/1</code> JSON lines identical to <code>kshana connect map</code>. See <a href="https://github.com/ashfordeOU/kshana/blob/main/docs/CONNECT.md"><code>docs/CONNECT.md</code></a>.</td>
+</tr>
+<tr>
 <td><code>export_test_bench</code></td>
 <td>A scenario&#39;s vehicle motion and events for a laboratory GNSS simulator (<code>kshana bench-export</code>): motion CSV and JSON, NMEA, waypoints and events as text, nothing written to disk. Kinds <code>gnss-ins</code>, <code>jamming</code>, <code>gnss-sim</code>. No signal: nothing exported is, models or drives a radio-frequency or baseband signal; the simulator and its operator supply the signals. See <a href="/docs/test-bench"><code>docs/TEST-BENCH.md</code></a>.</td>
 </tr>
