 <h2 id="kind-lunar-station-coverage">lunar-station-coverage<a class="anchor" href="#kind-lunar-station-coverage" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>
 <p>Modelled lunar reference-station coverage: a Monte Carlo sweep of the lunar differential-PNT model over a south-polar user grid and a day of epochs. A differential reference station at a known south-polar site corrects a stated constellation (illustrative Keplerian or a tabulated ephemeris) with a stated signal-in-space error, survey error, correction latency and link quantization; per point and over the region it reports the percentile corrected and uncorrected position error (3-D, horizontal, vertical), availability, coverage against a stated threshold, DO-229E protection levels, the coverage radius per azimuth and the correction-link budget at the station and at the worst point. Not a statement about the performance of any real system; not affiliated with or endorsed by any agency. MODELLED.</p>
