+<h4 id="importing-a-simulator-motion-file">Importing a simulator motion file</h4>
+<p><code>kshana::interop::testbench::read_sim_motion</code> reads the two gps-sdr-sim motion layouts back into
+Kshana motion samples: <code>Ecef</code> (<code>time, x, y, z</code>, the <code>-u</code> layout) and <code>Llh</code> (<code>time, latitude, longitude, height</code>, the <code>-x</code> layout). So a trajectory that was prepared for, or recorded from, a
+simulator can be scored or replayed in Kshana.</p>
+<ul>
+<li>Velocity is the central difference of the positions (one-sided at the ends). On the bundled
+<code>gnss-ins</code> export it is within 0.08 m/s of the scenario&#39;s velocity, and the position comes back
+exact (<code>Ecef</code>) or within 0.2 mm (<code>Llh</code>) (<code>tests/interop_testbench.rs</code>).</li>
+<li>These layouts carry no attitude, so heading, pitch and roll are imported as zero. Do not read
+the imported heading as the vehicle&#39;s heading.</li>
+<li>The time column must increase. A line with fewer than four fields, or a field that is not a
+number, is an error that names the line.</li>
+<li>Other simulators&#39; scenario formats are not imported yet. Their formats are vendor documents, and
+each needs its own published sample and check first.</li>
+</ul>
