iven to both solvers in the full runs; the initial-step routine is compared separately. Not covered: RKF7(8), stiffness detection, event location</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/dop853_scipy_oracle.rs (8 single steps: state within 5.55e-15 relative, FSAL derivative 3.46e-15, dense output 1.99e-14, accept/reject decisions identical; 3 full runs at rtol = atol = 1e-12 (LEO 58000 s, e = 0.7…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="v" data-g="orbit"><summary><span class="st st-v">Validated</span><span class="lg-req">Robust Kepler-equation solver</span><code class="lg-mod">kepler,<wbr> <wbr>propagator</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Elliptic Kepler solver for all 0 &lt;= e &lt; 1 and all mean anomalies: Markley (1995) cubic starter and fifth-order correction, a cancellation-free residual (1-e)E + e(E - sin E) - M, and guarded Newton polishing (kepler::solve_kepler_markley, propagator::solve_kepler_robust)</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>mpmath 1.3.0 (BSD-3-Clause) 50-digit roots from the exact binary inputs. Bars pre-registered in xval/kepler-mpmath/PREREGISTRATION.md (df22174), stated relative to |E| with the e -&gt; 1, M -&gt; 0 conditioning argument; all met (xval/kepler-mpmath/RESULTS.md). The legacy solvers (solve_kepler_checked, orbit::solve_kepler, ephem::solve_kepler) are numerically unchanged, because committed outputs depend on them, and are not covered by this row</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/kepler_mpmath_oracle.rs (405 grid points, e from 0 to 0.999999, M in [-pi, pi] down to 1e-12: worst |E - E_ref| 0.898 eps|E| against a bar of 8 eps|E|; 9 wound-M points at worst 0.013 of their bar; no Newton…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="orbit"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">Range-rate and az/el batch orbit determination with station masking</span><code class="lg-mod">orbit_<wbr>determination <wbr>(determine_<wbr>orbit_<wbr>batch