inexEphemeris::<wbr>sv_<wbr>position_<wbr>ecef_<wbr>bds_<wbr>geo,<wbr> <wbr>NavParseOptions)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>BDS-SIS-ICD-B1I v3.0 §5.2.4.12 geostationary-satellite position from a broadcast ephemeris (inertial-like frame, then Rz(Ω̇e·tk)·Rx(−5°)), opt-in through the include_beidou_geo field of NavParseOptions, so the default reader still skips GEOs</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>Pre-registered (7aa264b, 110fef9) against an IGS MGEX precise orbit with the GEOs; no such product was reachable from the session that built it, so the comparison is pending and the row is MODELLED (checked against the published nominal GEO slots only)</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/bds_geo_broadcast_oracle.rs (real C01-C04 records: geostationary radius, longitudes 140.02/80.04/110.55/159.99 deg at the published slots, |latitude| 2.13 deg with the tilt vs 6.65 without; the pre-registered…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="v" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st st-v">Validated</span><span class="lg-req">SP3 precise-clock interpolation</span><code class="lg-mod">sp3 <wbr>(Sp3File::<wbr>clock_<wbr>s,<wbr> <wbr>clock_<wbr>nodes),<wbr> <wbr>precise_<wbr>products <wbr>(ClockRinex::<wbr>from_<wbr>sp3)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Satellite clock offset between the tabulated SP3 clock nodes by linear interpolation over the two bracketing valid nodes (the RTKLIB pephclk scheme; bad-clock sentinel skipped), and the same nodes fed to the precise-product chain as RINEX-clock-equivalent records</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>IGS final 30 s satellite clock combination (IGS0OPSFIN 30S CLK, 2025-02-24): published clock estimates at the query instants, not interpolated from the SP3; bars pre-registered in tests/fixtures/sp3_clock_igs_oracle/PREREGISTRATION.md before the first run (RMS 0.15 ns, p95 0.30 ns, node median 1e-12 s, discrimination 2x)</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/sp3_clock_igs_oracle.rs (IGS final 15 min SP3 of 2025-02-24 vs the IGS final 30 s clocks, 32 GPS satellites: node median |Δ| 2.6e-13 s; 3038 mid-point records RMS 0.121 ns, p95 0.265 ns; holding the node instead…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">Carrier-phase tightly coupled GNSS/INS with float ambiguities</span><code class="lg-mod">fusion::<wbr>carrier_<wbr>tc <wbr>(run_<wbr>carrier_<wbr>tc,<wbr> <wbr>CarrierTcCfg),<wbr> <wbr>fusion::<wbr>trajectory <wbr>(truth_<wbr>epochs)</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>Error-state EKF over 15 INS states, a two-state receiver clock and one float carrier ambiguity per tracked satellite; pseudorange, carrier phase and optional range rate from an SGP4 Walker constellation (light-time and Sagnac), Klobuchar and Saastamoinen/Niell corrections applied in the loop at the filter&#x27;s own position; time-differenced-carrier slip detection with a per-satellite threshold widened by the velocity uncertainty; ambiguity re-initialisation on slips and re-acquisition</dd><dt>Oracle</dt><dd>Internal consistency: the measurements are synthesised from the models the filter uses (χ² NEES/NIS over seeds, a noise-free convergence, slip injection). MODELLED; no real receiver data or third-party filter is compared</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>tests/fusion_carrier_tc.rs (figure-8 drive: steady 3-D RMS 0.025 m carrier vs 0.470 m code on identical measurements; 12 seeds mean NIS/dof 1.00 and steady NEES/dof 0.92; a 1-cycle slip detected at its epoch with no…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="orbit"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">GNSS/INS maritime, rail and aviation packs with a tight-coupling option</span><code class="lg-mod">fusion::<wbr>pack <wbr>(TightCfg,<wbr> <wbr>[tight]),<wbr> <wbr>scenarios <wbr><span class="nw">gnss-ins-maritime </span><wbr>/<wbr>