40 · 10^0.4 = 100.48 ns against the 100 ns plateau of G.812 Table 4). A standards transcription with internal consistency checks, not a conformance test and not an external validation. G.812 (06/2004) is listed as superseded by a pre-published 08/2026 edition and G.811 has an Amd. 1 (04/2016); neither could be read, so neither is checked. The free-running OCXO scenario overstates the oscillator&#x27;s contribution at observation intervals long against a loop&#x27;s time constant; it says nothing about any equipment clock</dd><dt>Tests</dt><dd><code>telecom_timing::tests (g811_prc_masks_follow_clause_6_1; g812_masks_follow_tables_3_4_6_and_7; g8262_masks_follow_tables_1_3_4_and_5; g8262_1_eeec_masks_follow_tables_1_and_3; a_linear_piece_is_evaluated_without_powf…</code></dd></dl></details><details class="lg-row" data-fl-item data-s="m" data-g="clock"><summary><span class="st st-m">Modelled</span><span class="lg-req">Clock-log formats (RINEX clock, TimeLab ASCII, TAPR TICC) read to a normalised phase series</span><code class="lg-mod">clock_<wbr>log <wbr>(read_<wbr>input,<wbr> <wbr>MeasuredPhaseReport,<wbr> <wbr>MEASURED_<wbr>UNITS,<wbr> <wbr>TELECOM_<wbr>LOG_<wbr>UNITS); <wbr>telecom_<wbr>timing <wbr>(SeriesInput::<wbr>clock_<wbr>log); <wbr>api <wbr>(clock <wbr>kind <wbr>[clock_<wbr>log])</code></summary><dl class="lg-body"><dt>Capability</dt><dd>clock_log::read_input: one parser layer that turns a RINEX clock file (AS/AR records of one named clock, versions 2 and 3.00 to 3.04), a TimeLab-style ASCII phase or frequency log, or a TAPR TICC timestamp or interval log into a uniform phase grid, with tau0 stated, from a header, or the median spacing, every gap, off-grid reading and duplicate counted, and a refuse, longest-run or linear gap policy; wired opt-in into the telecom-timing series (<code>[series.clock_log]</code>, adding a <code>clock_log</code> block) and the clock kind (<code>[clock_log]</code>, adding a <code>measured</code> block with ADEV, TDEV and MTIE, the