>It drives no radio and transmits nothing; its signal-level output is baseband IQ sample files for software receivers.</span></div></div><div class="not"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M5.6 5.6l12.8 12.8"/></svg><div>Not a hardware or certified GNSS receiver<span>Its software receiver (acquisition and tracking on recorded or generated IQ) is an analysis tool, not a navigation product.</span></div></div><div class="not"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M5.6 5.6l12.8 12.8"/></svg><div>Not a flight product<span>A study and trade-off instrument, every answer labelled Validated or Modelled.</span></div></div></div></article></div>
