al): from a site, a time and constellation presets, two-line element sets (`tle`, with a UTC `epoch`) or satellites given as azimuth/elevation or ECEF, which satellites are visible and which are hidden by the skyline, GDOP/PDOP/HDOP/VDOP/TDOP from the gnss_lib_py-checked DOP kernel, the east-north-up cofactor and covariance with one receiver clock per system (or one in common), and the horizontal error ellipse at one sigma and at a stated confidence for a stated UERE.</li><li><code>trust_telemetry</code>: Render a GNSS trust stream or a `receiver-trust` result as security telemetry text (`kshana trust-telemetry`, docs/TRUST-TELEMETRY.md), with the same encoders the command line uses: `prometheus` (the exposition of the final state), `cef` or `leef` (one RFC 5424 syslog line per band change, or per epoch with `syslog_all`; no timestamp, because no clock is read) or `otlp` (the OTLP/HTTP JSON metrics payload).</li><li><code>validate_scenario</code>: Pre-flight check of a Kshana scenario TOML: verify it parses as TOML and detect its scenario kind, without running it.</li><li><code>verify_evidence_pack</code>: Verify a signed evidence pack (`kshana evidence verify`): every file&#x27;s SHA-256 against the manifest, the hash chain, the Ed25519 signature, and with `public_key` (the signer&#x27;s key, from the signer by another route) that the signer is the one expected, and with `full_log` that the log you hold is the one the pack records and that the slice came from it.</li></ul></div></noscript><p class="mp-nojs">The recorded session plays here step by step.</p></div>
