e, geometry and class, lowest and final score, when the first untrusted epoch came) and the last `$PKSHT` sentence."},{"name":"attach_evidence_timestamp","does":"Bind an RFC 3161 timestamp token to an evidence pack (`kshana evidence attach-timestamp`), in memory: `files` is a pack as `create_evidence_pack` returns it, `token_base64` the bytes of the `.tsr` file from a timestamp authority."},{"name":"build_interference_map","does":"Build a GNSS interference map from openly licensed aircraft (ADS-B NIC/NACp) or ship (AIS) position reports given as CSV text (`kshana interference-map adsb|ais`)."},{"name":"compliance_mapping","does":"The static public-framework mapping (`kshana compliance-report --mapping` / `--sources`) as Markdown: one table per framework with each row's paraphrased ask, the Kshana outputs that support evidence for it and the gap the outputs do not close; or, with `sources` true, the source documents the tables cite with versions and URLs."},{"name":"compliance_report","does":"Fill the public-framework mapping from Kshana result documents (`kshana compliance-report`): which rows of six resilience frameworks and standards (the US DHS Resilient PNT framework v2.0, IMO guidance for ships, EASA guidance for aviation, NIS2 Article 21, EN 16803, NIST IR 8323r1) the runs given support evidence for, which they do not, and the gap each row keeps."},{"name":"create_evidence_pack","does":"Create a signed evidence pack for a window of a vessel's NMEA 0183 log (`kshana receiver-trust evidence`): the raw log bytes for the window, the configuration with every threshold, the per-epoch results and reasons, a self-contained summary page, and a manifest listing every file's SHA-256 with the full log's hash and a hash chain, signed with Ed25519."},{"name":"create_round_trip_pack","does":"Create the signed laboratory round-trip pack (`kshana evidence round-trip`, docs/spec/TEST-CONDITIONS.md): links by hash the scenario that produced the motion, the laboratory's `kshana.test-conditions/1` document, the receiver log and its score against the stated events, in a signed evidence pack whose `config.json` carries a `round_trip` block."},{"name":"export_interop","does":"Export a Kshana scenario in one interoperability format: `czml` (Cesium Language, for CesiumJS), `kml` (Keyhole Markup Language, for Google Earth and geographic information system tools), `geojson` (RFC 7946), `stk` (Systems Tool Kit ephemeris `.e`, one file per satellite) or `sigmf` (Signal Metadata Format recording of a `spectrum` scenario's synthesised samples)."},{"name":"export_oem","does":"Export an `orbit` scenario's propagated constellation as CCSDS OEM 2.0 ephemeris text — the inertial (TEME) state time series carrying position AND velocity, which flight-dynamics tools (GMAT / Orekit / STK) read."},{"name":"export_omm","does":"Export an `orbit` scenario's mean elements as a CCSDS 502.0-B-2 OMM (Orbit Mean-Elements Message) catalogue — one OMM per satellite."},{"name":"export_sp3","does":"Export an `orbit` scenario's propagated constellation as SP3-c precise-ephemeris text (the standard GNSS post-processing format)."},{"name":"export_table_csv","does":"Run a Kshana scenario and return its reproducibility table as CSV text — the byte-stable table the CLI writes as `<scenario>.table.csv` and the papers cite."},{"name":"export_test_bench","does":"Export a scenario's vehicle motion and events for a laboratory GNSS simulator (`kshana bench-export`, docs/TEST-BENCH.md): a motion CSV and its JSON description (Earth-fixed and geodetic position, velocity, attitude, UTC), NMEA 0183 GGA/RMC sentences, a waypoint text when the sample grid is millisecond-regular, and the scenario's events as CSV and as `[[events]]` TOML for a `receiver-trust` scenario."},{"name":"fit_imu_log","does":"Fit the sensor parameters of the `hybrid` and `fusion` scenarios from a stationary IMU log (`kshana imu-fit`, docs/MACHINE-INPUTS.md)."},{"name":"generate_training_nmea","does":"Generate synthetic 