 the end of\n#                the day. Beside it, a `leo-pvt` timing run disciplines the same TCXO class\n#                to the Iridium constellation (the public `iridium-stl` preset: 66\n#                satellites at 780 km, L-band bursts 25 to 34 dB above GPS), holding\n#                between passes, and converts system time to UTC (Coordinated Universal\n#                Time) with the broadcast offset. A `leo-pass` run of one Iridium pass over\n#                the site carries the geometry the campaign exports.\n#\n# The alarm is raised on the LEO-disciplined time error against the 1000 ns guard; it\n# stays down. The free-running error is shown for comparison and is not alarmed. Both\n# runs use the same oscillator noise (the engine's TCXO class); the deterministic\n# frequency offset and ageing are taken as calibrated at the loss of GNSS.\n#\n# NIST measured Iridium PNT timing receivers with a miniature atomic clock within 40 ns of\n# UTC(NIST) over 40 days (https://www.nist.gov/publications/validating-timing-performance-improvement-ionospheric-corrections-iridium-pnt-receivers);\n# the modelled figures are a consistency comparison with that, not a reproduction.\n# MODELLED.\nkind = \"campaign\"\ntitle = \"Critical infrastructure timing: holdover with LEO time\"\nseed = 20260929\n\n[timeline]\nstep_s = 300.0\n\n[[phases]]\nname = \"gnss-locked\"\nduration_s = 600.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nalarms = []\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nseed = 42\nthreshold_ns = 1000.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.time]\nstep_s = 10.0\nduration_s = 600.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.gnss]\nwindows = [{ t0 = 0.0, t1 = 600.0, state = \"nominal\" }]\n[phases.runs.scenario.clock_quantum]\nid = \"optical-sr-lattice\"\nprovenance = \"Strontium optical lattice clock, space-oriented goal sigma_y(1s)=1e-15 (arXiv:1503.08457); not flown. Not read by this campaign.\"\ny0 = 5.0e-17\nq_wf = 1.0e-30\nq_rw = 0.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.clock_classical]\nid = \"tcxo-class\"\nprovenance = \"The engine's TCXO class (EndRun Technologies disciplined-oscillator data sheet, basic TCXO, Allan deviation 2.0e-10 at 1 s): q_wf = (2e-10)^2, q_rw = 3*(2e-12)^2, the same PSDs the leo-pvt timing run uses for class tcxo\"\ny0 = 0.0\nq_wf = 4.0e-20\nq_rw = 1.2e-23\n\n[[phases]]\nname = \"gnss-denied\"\nduration_s = 86400.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nalarms = []\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nseed = 43\nthreshold_ns = 1000.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.time]\nstep_s = 300.0\nduration_s = 86400.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.gnss]\nwindows = [\n  { t0 = 0.0, t1 = 300.0, state = \"nominal\" },\n  { t0 = 300.0, t1 = 86400.0, state = \"denied\" },\n]\n[phases.runs.scenario.clock_quantum]\nid = \"optical-sr-lattice\"\nprovenance = \"Strontium optical lattice clock, space-oriented goal sigma_y(1s)=1e-15 (arXiv:1503.08457); not flown. Not read by this campaign.\"\ny0 = 5.0e-17\nq_wf = 1.0e-30\nq_rw = 0.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.clock_classical]\nid = \"tcxo-class\"\nprovenance = \"The engine's TCXO class (EndRun Technologies disciplined-oscillator data sheet, basic TCXO, Allan deviation 2.0e-10 at 1 s): q_wf = (2e-10)^2, q_rw = 3*(2e-12)^2, the same PSDs the leo-pvt timing run uses for class tcxo\"\ny0 = 0.0\nq_wf = 4.0e-20\nq_rw = 1.2e-23\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"leo_time_error_ns\", unit = \"ns\", t = \"timing.rows[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"timing.rows[0].series[].error_ns\" },\n  { channel = \"leo_time_sigma_ns\", unit = \"ns\", t = \"timing.rows[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"timing.rows[0].series[].sigma_ns\" },\n]\nalarms = [{ channel = \"leo_time_error_ns\", compare = \"abs_above\", threshold = 1000.0 }]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pvt\"\nmode = \"timing\"\nseed = 9\nduration_s = 86400.0\nstep_s = 30.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nlat_deg = 39.99\nlon_deg = -105.26\nheight_m = 1655.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.timing]\nclocks = [\"tcxo\"]\ncn0_offsets_db = [0.0]\nweek = 2436\ntow0_s = 172800.0\ntrace = true\n[phases.runs.scenario.timing.utc]\na0_s = 4.0e-9\na1_s_per_s = 1.0e-14\nt_ot_s = 147456.0\nwn_t = 2436\ndelta_t_ls_s = 18.0\nsigma_s = 5.0e-9\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system]]\nname = \"Iridium\"\nleo_preset = \"iridium-stl\"\nmask_deg = 15.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"iridium_pass_elevation_deg\", unit = \"deg\", t = \"satellites[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"satellites[0].series[].elevation_deg\" },\n]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pass\"\nname = \"Iridium pass over the substation\"\nepoch = \"2026-09-28T08:00:00\"\nduration_s = 900.0\nstep_s = 10.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nenvironment = \"ground\"\nlat_deg = 39.99\nlon_deg = -105.26\nheight_m = 1655.0\nmask_deg = 15.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.satellite]]\nid = \"Iridium-pass\"\nsystem = \"iridium-stl\"\nmax_elevation_deg = 70.0\ntca_s = 450.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.gnss]\nenabled = false\n","leo-vertical-5g-network-timing":"# LEO-PNT vertical: wireless networks, 5G/6G base-station timing.\n#\n# A 5G time-division-duplex (TDD) base station in Madrid needs its time within 1.5\n# microseconds of every other cell's (ITU-T G.8271 accuracy class 4 at the end\n# application; 1.1 microseconds at the network reference point, G.8271.1). Its\n# oven-controlled crystal oscillator (OCXO) is disciplined to GNSS. When GNSS is lost for\n# a day:\n#\n#   * the `telecom-timing` kind runs the operator's own holdover analysis of the OCXO\n#     (temperature cycling of 2 K, the kind's G.8271.1 and G.8272 budgets): the events mark\n#     when its time error crosses the 1100 ns network limit and the 1500 ns end-application\n#     limit;\n#   * a `leo-pvt` timing run disciplines the same class of oscillator to the Xona Pulsar X5\n#     signal (public signal table, arXiv 2509.19551; both published shells, 258 satellites\n#     at about 1080 km) and converts system time to UTC (Coordinated Universal Time) with\n#     the broadcast offset, holding between passes;\n#   * a `leo-pass` run of the four highest Pulsar passes over the site carries the geometry\n#     the campaign exports.\n#\n# The alarm is raised on the LEO-disciplined time error against the 1100 ns network limit.\n#\n# MODELLED: the two oscillator models are each kind's own (the telecom kind's OCXO with\n# temperature and ageing terms, the timing run's OCXO class noise), so the comparison is\n# between the two analyses, not one oscillator; the X5 range error is the preset's.\nkind = \"campaign\"\ntitle = \"5G base-station timing: holdover and LEO time\"\nseed = 20260929\n\n[timeline]\nstep_s = 300.0\n\n[[phases]]\nname = \"gnss-lost\"\nduration_s = 86400.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nevents = [\n  { label = \"OCXO holdover exceeds the 1100 ns network limit\", at = \"budgets[0].time_to_exceed_s\" },\n  { label = \"OCXO holdover exceeds the 1500 ns end-application limit\", at = \"budgets[1].time_to_exceed_s\" },\n]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"telecom-timing\"\nseed = 20260929\nmasks = [\"prtc-a\"]\n[phases.runs.scenario.holdover]\noscillator = \"ocxo\"\ngnss_loss_s = 0.0\nduration_s = 86400.0\nsample_interval_s = 1.0\nlocked_te_sigma_ns = 1.0\ninitial_frequency_offset = 0.0\ntemperature_amplitude_k = 2.0\ntemperature_period_s = 86400.0\nlocked_duration_days = 5.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.budgets]]\nname = \"network limit at reference point C\"\nmax_abs_te_ns = 1100.0\nsource = \"ITU-T G.8271.1 (2022) Amd. 3 (05/2025) clause 7.3.1 (max|TE_L|, compared unfiltered)\"\n[[phases.runs.scenario.budgets]]\nname = \"end application, accuracy class 4\"\nmax_abs_te_ns = 1500.0\nsource = \"ITU-T G.8271 (03/2020) Amd. 1 (08/2024) Table 1, class 4\"\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"leo_time_error_ns\", unit = \"ns\", t = \"timing.rows[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"timing.rows[0].series[].error_ns\" },\n  { channel = \"leo_time_sigma_ns\", unit = \"ns\", t = \"timing.rows[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"timing.rows[0].series[].sigma_ns\" },\n]\nalarms = [{ channel = \"leo_time_error_ns\", compare = \"abs_above\", threshold = 1100.0 }]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pvt\"\nmode = \"timing\"\nseed = 21\nduration_s = 86400.0\nstep_s = 60.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nlat_deg = 40.42\nlon_deg = -3.70\nheight_m = 650.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.timing]\nclocks = [\"ocxo\"]\ncn0_offsets_db = [0.0]\nweek = 2436\ntow0_s = 172800.0\ntrace = true\n[phases.runs.scenario.timing.utc]\na0_s = 4.0e-9\na1_s_per_s = 1.0e-14\nt_ot_s = 147456.0\nwn_t = 2436\ndelta_t_ls_s = 18.0\nsigma_s = 5.0e-9\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system]]\nname = \"Pulsar X5\"\nleo_preset = \"xona-pulsar\"\nsignal = \"X5\"\nmask_deg = 10.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"pulsar_pass_elevation_deg\", unit = \"deg\", t = \"satellites[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"satellites[0].series[].elevation_deg\" },\n]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pass\"\nname = \"Pulsar passes over the base station\"\nepoch = \"2026-09-28T08:00:00\"\nduration_s = 900.0\nstep_s = 10.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nenvironment = \"ground\"\nlat_deg = 40.42\nlon_deg = -3.70\nheight_m = 650.0\nmask_deg = 10.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.leo_constellation]]\nsystem = \"xona-pulsar\"\nbands = [\"X5\"]\nmax_satellites = 4\n[phases.runs.scenario.gnss]\nconstellation = \"galileo\"\nband = \"E1\"\n","leo-vertical-autonomous-vehicle":"# LEO-PNT vertical: autonomous vehicles, an urban canyon with a LEO layer.\n#\n# A car drives east through Munich. On the open road every satellite above 10 deg is\n# usable; in the urban canyon the buildings hide everything below 35 deg. Each phase runs\n# a `leo-pvt` joint fix (GPS, Galileo and a generic low Earth orbit (LEO) layer of 240\n# satellites at 1080 km, 53 deg, with a 0.25 m signal-in-space range error), comparing the\n# GNSS-only error with the fused GNSS + LEO error against a 1.5 m lane-level threshold,\n# and a `leo-pass` run of one LEO pass seen from the moving car (its geometry is what the\n# campaign exports).\n#\n# In the canyon GPS and Galileo keep 8 satellites above 35 deg and their geometry turns\n# poor; the LEO layer adds 4 to 5 more and cuts the mean error from about 5.8 m to about\n# 2.1 m, but a single elevation cut-off still leaves the fused error above the lane-level\n# threshold at about half the canyon epochs, where the alarm is raised.\n#\n# MODELLED: a building mask as a single elevation cut-off (no multipath, no\n# non-line-of-sight signals); representative LEO signal and range error. The\n# `automotive-urban-canyon` scenario covers the inertial side of the same drive.\nkind = \"campaign\"\ntitle = \"Autonomous vehicle in an urban canyon with a LEO layer\"\nseed = 20260929\n\n[timeline]\nstep_s = 10.0\n\n[[phases]]\nname = \"open-road\"\nduration_s = 600.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"gnss_error_m\", unit = \"m\", t = \"joint.epochs[].t_s\", y = \"joint.epochs[].error_gnss_m\" },\n  { channel = \"position_error_m\", t = \"joint.epochs[].t_s\", y = \"joint.epochs[].error_fused_m\" },\n  { channel = \"gnss_in_view\", unit = \"count\", t = \"joint.epochs[].t_s\", y = \"joint.epochs[].n_gnss\" },\n  { channel = \"leo_in_view\", unit = \"count\", t = \"joint.epochs[].t_s\", y = \"joint.epochs[].n_leo\" },\n]\nalarms = [{ channel = \"position_error_m\", compare = \"above\", threshold = 1.5 }]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pvt\"\nmode = \"joint\"\nseed = 3\nduration_s = 600.0\nstep_s = 10.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nlat_deg = 48.137\nlon_deg = 11.575\nheight_m = 520.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system]]\nname = \"GPS\"\npreset = \"gps-baseline\"\ncn0_dbhz = [35.0, 45.0]\nsisre_m = 0.6\nmask_deg = 10.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system]]\nname = \"Galileo\"\npreset = \"galileo\"\ncn0_dbhz = [35.0, 45.0]\nsisre_m = 0.3\nisb_ns = 12.0\nmask_deg = 10.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system]]\nname = \"Generic LEO\"\nrole = \"leo\"\ncarrier_hz = 1191.795e6\nchip_rate_hz = 10.23e6\ncn0_dbhz = [45.0, 58.0]\nsisre_m = 0.25\nisb_ns = 25.0\nmask_deg = 10.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system.shell]]\ntotal = 240\nplanes = 12\nphasing = 1\naltitude_km = 1080.0\ninclination_deg = 53.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"leo_pass_elevation_deg\", unit = \"deg\", t = \"satellites[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"satellites[0].series[].elevation_deg\" },\n]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pass\"\nepoch = \"2026-09-28T08:00:00\"\nduration_s = 600.0\nstep_s = 10.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nenvironment = \"ground\"\nlat_deg = 48.137\nlon_deg = 11.575\nheight_m = 520.0\nspeed_m_s = 14.0\nheading_deg = 90.0\nmask_deg = 10.0\nantenna = \"patch\"\n[[phases.runs.scenario.satellite]]\nid = \"LEO-1\"\nsystem = \"generic-leo\"\nbands = [\"L\"]\nmax_elevation_deg = 75.0\ntca_s = 300.0\naltitude_km = 1080.0\ninclination_deg = 53.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.gnss]\nconstellation = \"galileo\"\nband = \"E1\"\n\n[[phases]]\nname = \"urban-canyon\"\nduration_s = 900.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"gnss_error_m\", unit = \"m\", t = \"joint.epochs[].t_s\", y = \"joint.epochs[].error_gnss_m\" },\n  { channel = \"position_error_m\", t = \"joint.epochs[].t_s\", y = \"joint.epochs[].error_fused_m\" },\n  { channel = \"gnss_in_view\", unit = \"count\", t = \"joint.epochs[].t_s\", y = \"joint.epochs[].n_gnss\" },\n  { channel = \"leo_in_view\", unit = \"count\", t = \"joint.epochs[].t_s\", y = \"joint.epochs[].n_leo\" },\n]\nalarms = [{ channel = \"position_error_m\", compare = \"above\", threshold = 1.5 }]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pvt\"\nmode = \"joint\"\nseed = 3\nduration_s = 900.0\nstep_s = 10.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nlat_deg = 48.137\nlon_deg = 11.575\nheight_m = 520.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system]]\nname = \"GPS\"\npreset = \"gps-baseline\"\ncn0_dbhz = [35.0, 45.0]\nsisre_m = 0.6\nmask_deg = 35.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system]]\nname = \"Galileo\"\npreset = \"galileo\"\ncn0_dbhz = [35.0, 45.0]\nsisre_m = 0.3\nisb_ns = 12.0\nmask_deg = 35.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system]]\nname = \"Generic LEO\"\nrole = \"leo\"\ncarrier_hz = 1191.795e6\nchip_rate_hz = 10.23e6\ncn0_dbhz = [45.0, 58.0]\nsisre_m = 0.25\nisb_ns = 25.0\nmask_deg = 35.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.system.shell]]\ntotal = 240\nplanes = 12\nphasing = 1\naltitude_km = 1080.0\ninclination_deg = 53.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"leo_pass_elevation_deg\", unit = \"deg\", t = \"satellites[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"satellites[0].series[].elevation_deg\" },\n]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pass\"\nepoch = \"2026-09-28T08:00:00\"\nduration_s = 900.0\nstep_s = 10.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nenvironment = \"ground\"\nlat_deg = 48.137\nlon_deg = 11.575\nheight_m = 520.0\nspeed_m_s = 14.0\nheading_deg = 90.0\nmask_deg = 35.0\nantenna = \"patch\"\n[[phases.runs.scenario.satellite]]\nid = \"LEO-1\"\nsystem = \"generic-leo\"\nbands = [\"L\"]\nmax_elevation_deg = 80.0\ntca_s = 450.0\naltitude_km = 1080.0\ninclination_deg = 53.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.gnss]\nconstellation = \"galileo\"\nband = \"E1\"\n","leo-vertical-rail-maritime":"# LEO-PNT vertical: railway and maritime, the bundled maritime and rail scenarios plus LEO.\n#\n# Three phases reuse the engine's own maritime and rail scenarios unchanged and add a low\n# Earth orbit (LEO) positioning, navigation and timing (PNT) pass for the same platform:\n#\n#   strait-jammed  `maritime-strait-jamming` (a ship in the Gulf of Finland, a 17 dBW\n#                  broadband L1 jammer about 30 km away): the GNSS carriers fall below\n#                  the 25 dB-Hz floor. A `leo-pass` run of the same ship (maritime user,\n#                  8 m/s) tracks a generic LEO satellite (1080 km, 97 deg polar orbit)\n#                  in its S and C bands, which the L1 jammer does not reach.\n#   rail-tunnel    `rail-tunnel-coast` (a train at 44.4 m/s coasting on a tactical inertial\n#                  unit in a tunnel, no aiding): the event marks the moment its position\n#                  error reaches 2 m, the kind's own crossing time.\n#   rail-open      back in the open, a `leo-pass` run of the train (160 km/h east of\n#                  Hamburg) tracks a generic LEO satellite (1080 km, 97 deg) in its L\n#                  and S bands, the signals a re-acquiring receiver would use to end\n#                  the coast.\n#\n# The alarm follows the jamming kind's own rule (fewer than four GNSS satellites\n# tracking) in the strait. The jamming and LEO runs do not share a model: the leo-pass kind\n# has no jammer, and the S and C bands are outside the L1 jammer's 20 MHz by construction.\n# MODELLED.\nkind = \"campaign\"\ntitle = \"Railway and maritime with a LEO layer\"\nseed = 20260929\n\n[timeline]\nstep_s = 10.0\n\n[[phases]]\nname = \"strait-jammed\"\nduration_s = 1800.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"jamming\"\nseed = 1\nmask_deg = 5.0\ntracking_threshold_dbhz = 25.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.time]\nstep_s = 30.0\nduration_s = 1800.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.receiver]\nlat_deg = 59.80\nlon_deg = 24.90\nalt_m = 0.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.constellation]\naltitude_km = 20200.0\ninclination_deg = 55.0\nplanes = 6\nsats_per_plane = 4\nphasing_f = 1.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.jammer]\nposition_ecef_m = [2904623.523, 1381438.498, 5489328.347]\npower_dbw = 17.0\ngain_dbi = 0.0\njammer_type = \"broadband\"\nbandwidth_mhz = 20.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"leo_cn0_s_dbhz\", unit = \"dB-Hz\", t = \"satellites[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"satellites[0].series[].bands[0].cn0_dbhz\" },\n  { channel = \"leo_cn0_c_dbhz\", unit = \"dB-Hz\", t = \"satellites[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"satellites[0].series[].bands[1].cn0_dbhz\" },\n]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pass\"\nname = \"Ship in the Gulf of Finland\"\nepoch = \"2026-09-28T08:00:00\"\nduration_s = 900.0\nstep_s = 10.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nenvironment = \"maritime\"\nlat_deg = 59.8\nlon_deg = 24.9\nheight_m = 10.0\nspeed_m_s = 8.0\nheading_deg = 45.0\nmask_deg = 5.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.satellite]]\nid = \"LEO-1\"\nsystem = \"generic-leo\"\nbands = [\"S\", \"C\"]\nmax_elevation_deg = 75.0\ntca_s = 450.0\naltitude_km = 1080.0\ninclination_deg = 97.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.gnss]\nenabled = false\n\n[[phases]]\nname = \"rail-tunnel\"\nduration_s = 120.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nevents = [{ label = \"inertial coast error reaches 2 m\", at = \"crossings[0].coast_s\" }]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"ins-trn-coast\"\nimu_grade = \"tactical\"\nspeed_m_s = 44.4\nref_accel_m_s2 = 0.0\ncombination = \"rss\"\ncrossing_thresholds_m = [2.0, 20.0]\ndrift_band_lo_m_per_s = 0.001\ndrift_band_hi_m_per_s = 0.050\ntrn_fix_mode = \"none\"\nmission_duration_s = 600.0\n\n[[phases]]\nname = \"rail-open\"\nduration_s = 600.0\n\n[[phases.runs]]\nseries = [\n  { channel = \"leo_cn0_l_dbhz\", unit = \"dB-Hz\", t = \"satellites[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"satellites[0].series[].bands[0].cn0_dbhz\" },\n  { channel = \"leo_cn0_s_dbhz\", unit = \"dB-Hz\", t = \"satellites[0].series[].t_s\", y = \"satellites[0].series[].bands[1].cn0_dbhz\" },\n]\n[phases.runs.scenario]\nkind = \"leo-pass\"\nname = \"Train east of Hamburg\"\nepoch = \"2026-09-28T08:00:00\"\nduration_s = 600.0\nstep_s = 10.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.user]\nenvironment = \"ground\"\nlat_deg = 53.55\nlon_deg = 10.3\nheight_m = 20.0\nspeed_m_s = 44.4\nheading_deg = 90.0\nmask_deg = 5.0\n[[phases.runs.scenario.satellite]]\nid = \"LEO-1\"\nsystem = \"generic-leo\"\nbands = [\"L\", \"S\"]\nmax_elevation_deg = 70.0\ntca_s = 300.0\naltitude_km = 1080.0\ninclination_deg = 97.0\n[phases.runs.scenario.gnss]\nenabled = false\n"},"publish":["leo-pnt-mega-shell","lunar-relay-constellation","mars-orbit-pnt","europa-surface-pnt","campaign-shared-jammer-sea-road"]};
