+## tip-and-cue#
+
+MODELLED revisit and tip-and-cue latency of a two-layer maritime survey over the Baltic Sea: an RF survey layer and an optical layer, each a Walker star pattern of 550 km sun-synchronous orbits propagated with the secular J2 drift on a spherical Earth, with an elevation mask for the RF layer and an off-nadir field of regard (and optionally daylight) for the optical layer. Reports R, the area-weighted mean gap between RF accesses per point; F, the mean wait until every sea point has been in view; and Q, the mean wait from an RF access to an optical look, each with its median, 95th percentile and largest value. Geometry and timing only: no detection, weather or tasking latency. A cross-check of published simulation figures, never a validation.
+
+### tip-and-cue-baltic-m2.toml
+
+kind tip-and-cuenot matched to a ledger module by name
+
+M2 (docs/design/evidence/m2-revisit-tip-and-cue/PREREGISTRATION.md): revisit, full-area refresh and RF-to-optical reaction of a two-layer survey over the Baltic Sea, for the pre-registered primary cases (16 and 32 satellites per layer) and variants V1 to V4, over 7 days at a 10 s step. Readings: xval/m2-revisit-tip-and-cue/README.md. A cross-check of published simulation figures, never a validation. Takes a few seconds in a release build.
+
+```
+kind = "tip-and-cue"
+title = "M2: revisit and tip-and-cue latency over the Baltic Sea"
+area = "baltic"
+step_s = 10
+span_days = 7
+```
+
+Not yet on GitHub
+
+### tip-and-cue-short.toml
+
+kind tip-and-cuenot matched to a ledger module by name
+
+A short tip-and-cue run: the M2 primary 16-satellite RF layer cueing its optical layer over the Baltic Sea for 2 days at a 60 s step (fast; for the full pre-registered run see tip-and-cue-baltic-m2.toml). Geometry and timing only; MODELLED.
+
+```
+kind = "tip-and-cue"
+title = "Two-layer survey over the Baltic Sea, 2 days"
+step_s = 60
+span_days = 2
+name = "rf-16-optical-16"
+rf = { total = 16, planes = 8, phasing = 1, node_offset = 0.0 }
+rf_mask_deg = 10.0
+optical = { total = 16, planes = 8, phasing = 1, node_offset = 0.5 }
+```
