caping rests on the Logstash codec alone. The comparison bar was registered in commits 5172e579 (pycef) and 0a7598aa (Logstash) before either parser was run, and both met it at the first comparison. Five amendments are disclosed. Amendments (1) to (3) touched no comparison rule and no expected value: (1) a corpus-size assertion was corrected from 5 to 4 band changes, a miscount, since the stream has 4; (2) the Logstash runner's pipeline delimiter wiring was fixed after a first attempt that produced no events; (3) the trust score and epoch offset were moved from the CEF integer fields cn1 and cn2 to the floating-point fields cfp1 and cfp2, a wire-format change made in this release, after which the corpus was regenerated and both oracles were re-run with the bar unchanged and met it again. Amendment (4), 0.36, extended the corpus and the expected key set, registered in d6331429 before either parser ran on the new lines: schema 1.3 inputs add the satellite geometry in the custom fields cs6 (label geometry: status, then ';' and the deduction classes), cfp3 (geometryHdop) and cfp4 (geometryPdop); 13 geometry cases (the corpus to 170 lines) and the three new keys; both met the bar, otherwise unchanged, at the first comparison (pycef 166 of 170 lines parsed, the 4 tier 2 header cases as before; Logstash 170 of 170). Amendment (5), 0.36, appended 6 geometry-label cases (the corpus to 176 lines), registered in 9a8e4fa9 before either parser ran on them: from inputs that carry the geometry label, cs6 gains a third field (';' and the label) and cn1 (geometryUsedSatellites) the satellites used; the Logstash codec's mapping table was read first (no flexString fields, hence cs6 rather than flexString1); both met the bar at the first comparison (pycef 172 of 176, Logstash 176 of 176), and every earlier reference entry was reproduced unchanged. WHAT IS NOT: neither parser type-checks the cfp values (both keep them as text), so the use of the floating-point fields rests on the CEF dictionary rather than on an oracle; no vendor SIEM was run; the extension key names and their mapping are this crate's choice, and the parsers show only that they are read back as written; the RFC 5424 envelope, delivery, timeouts and reconnection are not covered; pycef is a small parser last released in 2020, and the Logstash codec is the more substantial oracle. |  VALIDATED |
