-Receiver-trust interference thresholds calibrated on the JammerTest 2024 dataset | receiver_trust::calibration::run_dataset: the pre-registered calibration of the C/N0-drop, AGC and jamming-indicator monitors on the public JammerTest 2024 dataset (Zenodo 15911589, GPL-3.0-or-later, fetched at run time, never vendored): per folder a 1 s timeline from mon_rf.csv and rinex.csv, the monitors run once, each post-calibration epoch labelled clean or jamming from the folder's attack_log (shifted from CEST to UTC, 60 s guard), every threshold swept over a fixed grid, the smallest threshold with pooled clean false-alarm probability at most 0.01 selected, and leave-one-folder-out held-out counts; a UBX reader cross-check. The selection ships only as the opt-in profile [monitors] profile = "jammertest-2024-calibrated" (cn0_drop_db 1.5, agc_k_sigma 3.5, jam_ind_threshold 29); the default rule and every output without it are unchanged | MODELLED | The dataset's published event logs (attack_log windows), as event truth, under the pre-registration xval/jammertest-trust/PREREGISTRATION.md (committed alone, 0fa012b, before the harness ran). First and only run (xval/jammertest-trust/RESULTS.md): 14 of 24 folders evaluable (7 with jamming), 3,502 clean and 9,560 jamming epochs. Held-out clean false-alarm probability: cn0_drop_db 0.0231 (81/3502) against a 0.02 bar, FAIL; agc_k_sigma 0.0003, pass; jam_ind_threshold 0.0094, pass; union of the three: false alarms 0.0328, detection 0.807 against 0.05 and 0.50, pass. By the registered rule the row is MODELLED (one bar failed). Narrow: one receiver type (u-blox ZED-F9P), one event, scheduled one-minute slots as truth (detection a lower bound; clean means outside the logged windows); calibrated on the CSV logs, and the UBX reader gives more false alarms on two folders. Maritime trust-score bands are not calibrated | receiver_trust::calibration (run_dataset); receiver_trust::monitors (MonitorConfig::profile, JAMMERTEST_2024_CALIBRATED); realdata::jammertest; examples/jammertest_trust_calibration.rs |
