-Calibration of the open receiver's C/N0 and lock models to IQ campaign results, with stated prediction error |  iq::labfit (campaign, cn0, iqfit, iqreport) and [input] campaign on kshana iq labfit, Python kshana.iq_labfit and the MCP labfit tool (campaign folders inside its work directory only): reads a kshana iq campaign output folder by its DIGEST and groups the scored cells into fit units (signal x loop design x front-end chain x jammer type, never pooled). Per unit, it fits measured C/N0 against stated J/S with the spectral-separation form. Q_eff is not identifiable from C/N0 data without an independent measurement of the jammer and signal powers, so Q is stated, never fitted (the type table, the event's q, or for an unknown type the most damaging stated value, cw Q = 1). The fitted parameter is the identifiable offset delta_eff = delta - 10 log10 Q, with the correlation guard reporting the degeneracy. C/N0 bins locked under 90 % are censored and listed. The threshold J/S is given directly and by the closed form; the tracking-loop and empirical lock models are coupled through the C/N0 model, with drop and re-lock dwells. A seeded cluster bootstrap over recordings (1000 replicates) gives percentile intervals; 90 % prediction intervals come from residual draws; leave-one-recording-out hold-outs are split into interpolation and extrapolation; a pre-registered [validation] table is hashed and each bar judged PASS/FAIL. Report kshana.labfit-iq/1 as JSON, CSV and generated Markdown, with a units block. Synthetic only (no third-party recording, no jammer waveform). The receiver-log labfit path is unchanged |  InternalConsistency |  checked against its own closed-form / analytic identity — catches transcription and coefficient errors, but is not an external oracle — Synthetic parameter recovery on Kshana's own GPS L1 C/A scenes with a known C/N0 profile imposed from the section 3.1 formula, tracked and scored by kshana iq campaign, against bars pre-registered in docs/design/LABFIT-FROM-IQ.md (section 5.1, amended 2026-10-12 in b7117bf, section 13). The campaigns' C/N0 estimator (M2M4) was fixed in 5b13e3c2, pushed before the first bar evaluation (committed together with the fit code, not alone), after one disclosed diagnostic tracking run. FINDING on the 18-event bar campaign: (c) PASS; (a') NOT MET, delta_eff error -1.097 dB against 0.5 dB (still -0.89 dB on bins at 38 dB-Hz and above); (b') NOT MET, 0 of 50 campaigns cover the truth (error -1.189 +/- 0.093 dB, interval about 0.3 dB); (d) NOT MET, closed form 2.20 dB below the direct J/S at loss, about the fitted drop dwell times the ramp rate (2.09 dB); the original Q clauses of (a) and (b) are NOT MET because Q is not identifiable. FOLLOW-UP (bars pre-registered in 1e532f84, docs/design/evidence/labfit-followup/RESULTS.md): on a stepped-J/S campaign delta_eff is recovered within +0.185 dB (S1 MET: the ramp error is estimator lag); (d) as written on it is met by the tracking-loop model (0.45 dB) but not the empirical one (6.42 dB), so S2 is NOT MET; on a fresh ramp campaign (d) with the fitted drop dwell times each event's ramp rate added is within 1 dB for both models (R1 MET), and (a') and (d) as written miss again (-1.25 dB; 2.32 and 9.47 dB). The method is checked, not any receiver: it cannot be VALIDATED from synthetic data |  iq::labfit (campaign, cn0, iqfit, iqreport, schema, mod); iq::cli::labfit |  tests/iq_labfit_campaign.rs: bar_c_holdout_prediction_intervals_cover_between_80_and_98_percent (PI90 coverage 0.891 over 558 bins, 0.900 over 10 time-to-loss events under each lock model), the_report_carries_its_inputs_censoring_validation_and_labels (inputs, censoring, [validation] hash and verdicts, units block audit), the_cluster_bootstrap_reproduces_from_the_campaign_and_seed, a_validation_mode_fit_refuses_to_start_without_its_table; bar_a_prime_delta_eff_is_recovered_and_q_is_stated_not_fitted, bar_d_closed_form_threshold_matches_the_direct_estimate_within_1_db and bar_b_prime_ci_subset (strict, ignored with the gap); bar_b_prime_full_set_of_50_campaigns (ignored, run before release); iq::labfit::cn0 tests (exact Q-delta degeneracy, delta recovery at the stated Q, closed-form threshold inverse); iq::labfit::iqfit tests (the lock-model conditions reproduce the C/N0 model exactly); tests/iq_labfit_followup.rs (the follow-up registered in 1e532f84: s1_delta_eff_on_the_stepped_campaign MET, s2_d_as_written_on_the_stepped_campaign asserting the recorded NOT MET, r1_dwell_corrected_d_on_the_fresh_ramp_campaign MET, in release) |
