-Lunar terrain horizon masks from a stated profile or a polar DEM |  Per-site azimuth-dependent horizon masks for the lunar-station-coverage kind (the reference station and every user point) and the moonlight-service-volume grid and its per-satellite export site (each export row gains clears_terrain), in the 0.36 skyline table format (skyline::Skyline, linear in azimuth with wrap at 360 deg; a stated profile and a DEM horizon at one site combine as their pointwise maximum): a stated [terrain] station_horizon or user_horizon labelled with its source, and/or a horizon ray-marched over a south polar stereographic DEM (the LRO LOLA gridded polar layout, read from a descriptor that fixes its size and SHA-256, or a latitude/longitude realdata::lola_dem tile with [terrain] dem_tile_path, echoed with its SHA-256) along great circles of the lunar sphere with exact curvature, from a stated mast height, at a stated azimuth step and range. A satellite counts at a site when it clears the flat mask_deg and the horizon at its azimuth (lunar_service::topocentric); an epoch the horizon leaves with fewer than four satellites at a point, where the flat mask gives four, is counted as the unavailable reason terrain_masked. The vendored DEM is a crop of the public-domain LOLA LDEM_75S_240M product, 5 x 5 block-mean resampled to 1200 m (data/lunar-dem/NOTICE.md). Absent, every site keeps the flat mask and every document is byte-identical |  InternalConsistency |  checked against its own closed-form / analytic identity — catches transcription and coefficient errors, but is not an external oracle — Closed-form surfaces (InternalConsistency): the bare-sphere dip, a crater in a plateau on the sphere with an observer on and off its centre, and an analytic cone against its own rasterisation. On the real crop, an independent numpy ray-cast (scripts/gen_lunar_terrain_ref.py, numpy 2.5.3; pre-registered in tests/fixtures/lunar_terrain/PREREGISTRATION.md, committed alone in edbb9b02 before the scri