 Lunar reference-station multipath and receiver-hardware terms |  The optional [receiver] section of lunar-station-coverage (LRS-02): elevation-dependent multipath sigma(el) = a + b exp(-el / el0) at the user and at the station (the RTCA DO-229 airborne functional form, its a = 0.13 m, b = 0.53 m, el0 = 10 deg as defaults; on the Moon every value is ILLUSTRATIVE), white at the user and first-order Gauss-Markov over epochs at the station (rho = exp(-dt / tau)); early-minus-late DLL thermal code noise sigma = L_c sqrt(B_L d / (2 C/N0) (1 + 2 / ((2 - d) T C/N0))); per-channel inter-channel biases constant over a trial, at the user and at the station. Station terms enter its corrections, user terms the raw and corrected measurements, each on its own seeded stream. Absent, every document is unchanged |  InternalConsistency |  checked against its own closed-form / analytic identity — catches transcription and coefficient errors, but is not an external oracle — Closed forms and statistics of the model's own draws (InternalConsistency): the DLL formula against a hand computation, the DO-229 form, the zero-baseline difference of two receivers, the Gauss-Markov lag-1 correlation. No lunar multipath or receiver measurement exists to compare with; the values are ILLUSTRATIVE and nothing here is a statement about any real receiver |  lunar_receiver; lunar_station |  lunar_receiver::tests (multipath_is_the_do229_form; dll_noise_matches_a_hand_computation: 0.825279 m at 45 dB-Hz, 0.5 Hz, d = 1, 20 ms; bad_sections_are_refused); tests/lunar_station_ext.rs (receiver_absent_or_silent_is_the_plain_run; zero_baseline_multipath_is_the_difference_of_two_receivers: sample sigma sqrt(2) a within 6 %; station_multipath_is_gauss_markov: lag-1 correlation exp(-dt / tau) within 0.01, unit variance within 2 %; inter_channel_biases_are_constant_over_a_trial); tests/prediction_frozen.rs and the goldens unchanged (additivity) |
 
