ents a user and the station share four satellites above 5 deg in only 8.2 % (300 km) and 6.3 % (600 km) of epochs, at near-singular geometry (uncorrected p95 3.8 km against the sources' < 10 m). The sources' simulations used a filter, a height constraint and three satellites in common view, which the snapshot kind does not model. The comparison therefore neither confirms nor refutes the published 'sub-metre over the whole south pole'. It shows that this model's result depends on orbits that are not published. Not a statement about any real system; not affiliated with or endorsed by any agency |  lunar_station (over lunar_dpnt, lunar_service) |  tests/lunar_station_published_oracle.rs::recorded_finding_one_of_six_bars_passes (the recorded figures against the registered bars); tests/lunar_station_published_oracle.rs::published_claims_comparison_run (ignored, about 7 s in release: re-runs the six registered cases and asserts the recorded figures) |
