+# Space RF survey (scenario kind family)
+
+1 scenario kind of the engine v0.40.0. Advisory: analysis output from a research and engineering tool, not type-approved navigation equipment and not a safety-of-life service. Every label here is the engine's or the verification matrix's; a kind is MODELLED unless the matrix says otherwise (how a label is earned: the README's Evidence section).
+
+Topic pages: TIP-AND-CUE. Run one: kshana scenarios/tip-and-cue-baltic-m2.toml. All families: KINDS.md.
+
+Kind |  What it does |  Ledger |
+
+tip-and-cue |  MODELLED revisit and tip-and-cue latency of a two-layer maritime survey over the Baltic Sea: an RF survey layer and an optical layer, each a Walker star pattern of 550 km sun-synchronous orbits propag |  MODELLED (result label) |
+
+### tip-and-cue#
+
+MODELLED revisit and tip-and-cue latency of a two-layer maritime survey over the Baltic Sea: an RF survey layer and an optical layer, each a Walker star pattern of 550 km sun-synchronous orbits propagated with the secular J2 drift on a spherical Earth, with an elevation mask for the RF layer and an off-nadir field of regard (and optionally daylight) for the optical layer. Reports R, the area-weighted mean gap between RF accesses per point; F, the mean wait until every sea point has been in view; and Q, the mean wait from an RF access to an optical look, each with its median, 95th percentile and largest value. Geometry and timing only: no detection, weather or tasking latency. A cross-check of published simulation figures, never a validation.
+
+Required fields: none. Optional: kind, title, seed, area, step_s, span_days, m2, cases.
+
+Ledger: no matrix row names this kind; the engine labels its own result. Full page, with the inputs, results, evidence and limitations: tip-and-cue.
+
+```
+kshana scenarios/tip-and-cue-short.toml
+```
