-{"engine_version":"0.40.0","file":"leo-band-trade.toml","toml":"# LEO-PNT band trade, UHF to wide C band: what a low Earth orbit (LEO) positioning,\n# navigation and timing (PNT) signal gains and loses in each band, independent of any\n# particular system.\n#\n# Five REPRESENTATIVE designs from the compiled-in `generic-bands` preset, each a pilot\n# and data pair with a 50/50 power split sized to its band:\n#   UHF   465 MHz,      BPSK(5) in 10 MHz\n#   L     1191.795 MHz, BPSK(10) in 20.46 MHz (the Galileo E5 centre)\n#   S     2492.028 MHz, BPSK(5) in 16.5 MHz (the NavIC S-band carrier, in the RDSS band)\n#   C     5020 MHz,     BPSK(10) in 20 MHz (the middle of the 5010-5030 MHz RNSS band)\n#   wide C 5100 MHz,    BPSK(50) in 120 MHz\n# (BPSK binary phase-shift keying; RDSS Radio Determination Satellite Service; RNSS Radio\n# Navigation Satellite Service.)\n#\n# The trade table puts four things side by side:\n#   * ionospheric delay: first order, 40.3 TEC / f^2, for a 50 TECU slant total electron\n#     content: UHF carries (1191.795/465)^2 = 6.6 times the L-band delay, C band 0.056;\n#   * free-space loss at a 1000 km slant range: +20 log10(f/f_L) dB relative to L;\n#   * ranging accuracy (delay-lock-loop thermal-noise jitter, 0.5 chip coherent\n#     early-late spacing, 1 Hz loop) at equal C/N0 (45 dB-Hz for all), and at equal\n#     radiated power (C/N0 falls with the free-space loss: isotropic antennas at both\n#     ends, so the higher band's smaller receive aperture is charged in full);\n#   * the J/S a CW tone, wideband noise and matched noise may reach before the tracked\n#     pilot falls below 25 dB-Hz, at the equal-power C/N0.\n# MODELLED: the closed forms are validated; the designs, the TEC, the range and the\n# equal-power assumption are inputs. No rain or atmospheric loss (it matters at C band).\nkind = \"leo-signal\"\npresets = [\"generic-bands\"]\n\n[receiver]\nnoise_figure_db = 2.0\nantenna_temp_k = 290.0\ncn0_dbhz = [30.0, 35.0, 40.0, 45.0, 50.0, 55.0]\nreference_cn0_dbhz = 45.0\nloop_bandwidth_hz = 1.0\nintegration_time_s = 0.02\ncorrelator_spacings_chips = [1.0, 0.5, 0.2, 0.1]\nreference_spacing_chips = 0.5\ntracking_threshold_dbhz = 25.0\n\n[acquisition]\naltitude_km = 550.0\noscillator_ppm = 0.5\ncoherent_ms = 1.0\nnoncoherent = 1\npfa_cell = 1e-4\n\n[trade]\nreference_signal = \"generic-l\"\nslant_tec_tecu = 50.0\nslant_range_km = 1000.0\n","summary":"scenario leo-signal | 5 signals | noise floor -202.0 dBW/Hz | finest ranging generic-c-wide 0.022 m at 45.0 dB-Hz","json":"{\n  \"engine_version\": \"0.40.0\",\n  \"kind\": \"leo-signal\",\n  \"label\": \"MODELLED: parameterised low Earth orbit (LEO) positioning, navigation and timing (PNT) signal designs, band-limited to their transmit bandwidth. The closed forms underneath are VALIDATED (BPSK power in band and Gabor bandwidth, the band-limited early-late code-tracking jitter reducing to the textbook forms, the offset spectral separation coefficient, and the maximum LEO Doppler against Xona Pulsar and Iridium figures); every signal design, power split, C/N0 and jammer level is an input, and a preset marked WORKSHOP or REPRESENTATIVE is not a published specification.\",\n  \"not_modelled\": [\n    \"the exact spectra of enhanced Feher QPSK, code shift keying and OFDM: a rectangular-chip BPSK envelope or a flat band stands in, as each preset states\",\n    \"spreading-code line structure and multiple-access cross-correlation between codes\",\n    \"the transmit and receive filters beyond an ideal brick wall at the transmit bandwidth: no out-of-band emission, no filter group delay\",\n    \"multipath, receiver quantisation and automatic gain control\",\n    \"Earth rotation in the Doppler bound (up to about 0.46 km/s of range rate at the equator)\",\n    \"ionospheric delay beyond first order, and the split of the electron content above and below a LEO satellite: the slant TEC is an input\",\n    \"atmospheric, rain and polarisation losses: the free-space loss alone is compared (rain matters at C band)\",\n    \"acquisition beyond a single dwell with a false-alarm penalty: no multi-dwell verification logic, a uniform code-phase prior, the worst-case straddle\",\n    \"aggregate interference beyond a per-satellite count: one GNSS satellite unless compatibility.gnss_aggregate_satellites says otherwise, one LEO satellite\"\n  ],\n  \"receiver\": {\n    \"antenna_temp_k\": 290.0,\n    \"cn0_dbhz\": [\n      30.0,\n      35.0,\n      40.0,\n      45.0,\n      50.0,\n      55.0\n    ],\n    \"correlator_spacings_chips\": [\n      1.0,\n      0.5,\n      0.2,\n      0.1\n    ],\n    \"early_late\": \"coherent\",\n    \"integration_time_s\": 0.02,\n    \"loop_bandwidth_hz\": 1.0,\n    \"noise_density_dbw_per_hz\": -201.9751871942281,\n    \"noise_figure_db\": 2.0,\n    \"reference_cn0_dbhz\": 45.0,\n    \"reference_spacing_chips\": 0.5,\n    \"system_temp_k\": 459.61902581372294,\n    \"tracking_threshold_dbhz\": 25.0\n  },\n  \"scenario_hash\": \"34a6b3211c13ec395ced66f24352cb1fb212d427b837d94f74c73e816ef00edd\",\n  \"shape_checks\": [],\n  \"shape_checks_pass\": true,\n  \"signals\": [\n    {\n      \"acquisition\": {\n        \"acquisition_cn0_dbhz\": 41.98970004336019,\n        \"cells\": 358050.0,\n        \"code_bin_chips\": 0.5,\n        \"code_bins\": 10230.0,\n        \"coherent_s\": 0.001,\n        \"coherent_snr_db\": 11.989700043360187,\n        \"component\": \"pilot\",\n        \"doppler_bin_hz\": 666.6666666666666,\n        \"doppler_bins\": 35.0,\n        \"dwell_s\": 0.001,\n        \"elevation_mask_deg\": 0.0,\n        \"max_doppler_satellite_hz\": 10831.043019078488,\n        \"mean_time_code_parallel_s\": 0.8840434713259993,\n        \"mean_time_serial_s\": 1252.789804855195,\n        \"modulation\": \"BPSK(5)\",\n        \"noncoherent\": 1,\n        \"orbit_altitude_m\": 550000.0,\n        \"oscillator_doppler_hz\": 232.5,\n        \"pd_no_straddle\": 0.9241692493793363,\n        \"pd_worst_straddle\": 